# Project Closure Report (Draft)

INTERNAL: Software Corp use only. Not for distribution to the city.

Project: Smart Parking Platform
Prepared by: Tim Duncan, Project Manager
Version: 0.8 (draft)
Planned go-live: December 8, 2026

# 1. Executive Summary

Smart Parking Platform is a cloud-based parking solution for the city. A driver application (Mobile and Web) and an operator dashboard using a single backend system to provide real time occupancy data. The project will run from September 1st to December 8th 2026. It has 13 members and has an approved budget of $488,336, which includes a 15% contingency of $63,696.

Planning has been completed consistently. The requirements have been defined with 18 use cases, a WBS covering all required elements, a Gantt chart detailing dependencies and six milestones. A risk register with 12 risks has been created along with a communication and costing plan. Sprints 1 and 2 have been created in Jira. Final schedule and cost performance will be added at closure.

The 4 High risks remain open and are the biggest factors affecting the project outcome. These include: Occupancy Sensor API (R-01), Payment Sandbox Access (R-05), Compressed QA Window (R-06) and Late discovery of PCI-DSS issues (R-12).

