# 5. Lessons Learned

Communication
- Thirteen people means 78 possible communication paths. Keeping most conversation inside a team or a scheduled meeting is what made that workable
- Different readers need different reports. The city wants milestones, cost, and High risks. Developers want the board and the blockers
- Most of the gaps we found were between documents, so cross-checking them is part of communication

Testing and quality
- Test environments and the CI/CD pipeline belong early. We moved them into Sprint 2 after seeing R-11
- Releases go through staging with automated regression tests and a rollback plan. The Knight Capital case from earlier in the course is the reason
- QA starts early and has a buffer week before deployment, because the QA phase is the one that gets squeezed when anything upstream runs late (R-06)

Planning and management
- Dependencies need a direction check. A finish-start link nested in the wrong task moves the whole schedule
- Risk levels come from the matrix, not from adding probability and impact
- Early requests for sandbox access and firm feedback deadlines cost nothing and protect the schedule (R-05, R-10)
- The stakeholder grid put the city, the operators, and the development teams in "manage closely", so they get the most direct reporting

# 6. Recommendations for Future Projects

- Plan compliance and legal reviews before the work they could invalidate, not after. For payments, run the PCI-DSS design review in the first month and the full review before integration starts
- Request partner and vendor sandbox access on day one, in the contract if possible
- Put environments, CI/CD, and test data in the first sprint
- Check the cost plan, the schedule, the RACI, and the backlog against each other at every update, using one checklist
- Build a manual fallback for any feature that depends on a partner's data, as we did with manual occupancy entry (UC-18)
- Review the risk register every week and escalate any new High risk the same day
- Keep a central lessons learned file and add to it at the end of every sprint, not only at closure
- Hold the final retrospective with the whole team and publish a short version to the city

